event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":91,"item_id":"rs_0c94e5a77a807e72016aca39fe770c8194bccbc9b9412d1bb6","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering column migration**\n\nI’m thinking about how to handle the ordering column migration. It’s important to preserve the order of IDs during this process. I’ll need to ensure that when I insert a new row, it follows the max ID plus one. To achieve this, I should use an atomic single UPDATE with a subquery to find the maximum position for the new insertion. This should remain consistent across the project, and testing the migration will be essential."}

